WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
Primitive tokens tell you what a value is.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.940
Semantic tokens tell you what it is for.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.220
That second layer is what
makes theming, rebrands,

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.120
and dark mode manageable.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.740
You will keep components on role names, and
swap only the mapping when the theme changes.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.400
If a button uses teal-500 directly,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.980
dark mode means finding every
component that uses teal and deciding,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.480
one by one, what it should become.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.540
The component knows too
much about the palette.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.040
A semantic token describes
the role instead: surface,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.080
border, text, accent, focus.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.380
Components use only semantic tokens.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.240
Primitives are referenced
only inside the token layer.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:49.580
Dark mode becomes a new mapping,
not a new set of components.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.020
The media query follows
the operating system.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.980
The data-theme attribute
lets a person override it.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.960
The selector skips the dark mapping
when someone has pinned light.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.580
The accent shifts to a lighter teal in dark
mode so it keeps enough contrast against

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:12.650
a dark surface. A colour that works on
white can be too dark on near-black.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.360
Before, the badge hard-coded its colours
and needed a separate dark class.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.160
After, it has one rule
and works in both themes,

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:25.980
because surface-subtle and text point
somewhere else when the theme changes.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:30.120
Good semantic names describe
role and, when needed,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.880
state. Text muted. Border strong.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.160
Accent hover. Avoid names
that describe appearance,

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:43.720
like light grey, because the name stops
making sense the moment the theme changes.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.960
Keep the layer small. If you find yourself
creating a token for the settings page

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.620
card border, a variable inside
that component is a better home.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.560
Components consume semantic tokens.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.520
Only the token layer touches primitives.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.580
Themes are alternate mappings from
semantic names to primitive values.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:10.020
Name by role and state, not by
appearance, and keep the layer small.
